# See core/deb/indi-stable-core.lintian-overrides for the fuller reasoning;
# same mechanism, applied to the compiled Python extension this package
# ships instead of a server/driver binary.
#
# No dir-or-file-in-opt override needed here, unlike every other component in
# this project: this package deliberately installs to the ordinary system
# Python location, not /opt/indi-stable -- see DESIGN.md, "pyindi-client --
# packaging decisions" for why that is not an exception to the coexistence
# rule. If that tag ever appears for this package, something has changed and
# it should be investigated, not blanket-overridden.

# RPATH into the private libdir is the mechanism that stops _PyIndi*.so
# resolving against -- or being resolved against -- a distribution
# libindiclient.so carrying the same SONAME. Removing it breaks the
# coexistence guarantee.
indi-stable-pyindi-client: custom-library-search-path
